---
title: Better no-knead bread
servings: 6
yield: 1 loaf
tags: [no-knead, make-ahead, vegan]
cuisine: american
time: 87 hours 5 minutes
source: Better No-Knead Bread by J. Kenji López-Alt, Serious Eats, https://www.seriouseats.com/better-no-knead-bread-recipe
nutrition:
  calories: 182 kcal
---

Whisk the @bread flour{300%g}, @salt{4.5%g} and @instant yeast{3%g} together in a #large bowl{}. Add the @water{210%g} and stir until no dry flour is left.

Cover tightly and leave at room temperature ~{12%hours}, or up to 24 hours.

Move the bowl to the fridge for at least ~{3%days} and up to 5 days.

Tip the dough onto a well-floured counter, fold it over once or twice and shape it into a loaf. Cover with a floured towel and let it rise at room temperature ~{2%hours}, or up to 4 hours.

Meanwhile, set a rack in the lower-middle of the oven, put a #Dutch oven{} on it and heat to 450°F (230°C).

Cut 2 or 3 slashes 1/2 inch deep across the top. Lift the hot pot out, drop the loaf in, cover and bake ~{15%minutes}.

Uncover and bake ~{30%minutes} to 45 minutes more, until the middle reads 209°F (98°C).

Lift the loaf onto a #wire rack{} and let it cool at least ~{15%minutes} before slicing.

> Wrapped in foil it keeps 3 days at room temperature; crisp it in a hot oven or toaster.
